      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Spivey's development was closely tied to the arrival of the railroad, which facilitated settlement and commerce in the late 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/spivey_kansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office was established on December 6, 1886, initially under the name Leland before being renamed Spivey to align with the town's designation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/spivey_kansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The river's confluence with Sand Creek occurs near the community, contributing to the dissection of the surrounding landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/spivey_kansas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The annual average temperature in Spivey is approximately 56°F (13°C), shaped by strong continental climate influences that bring marked seasonal variations.",
